WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:06.000
“That which does not kill us makes us stronger”,
Friedrich Nietzsche famously wrote.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.200
In this Sprouts special in collaboration with
Stephen Hicks, we explore Nietzsche’s division

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:18.500
of the world into sheep and wolves, and how
our morality, what we consider as good and

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.660
bad, is the result of brute biological events.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:33.309
PART 2
“Sheep and Wolves”

00:00:33.309 --> 00:00:39.829
Nietzsche says: All of organic nature is divided
into these two types of species— those who

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:46.430
are naturally herd animals and those who are
naturally loners — those who are prey and

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:49.530
those who are predators.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:57.590
Psychologically and physically, this divide
also runs right through the human species.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:03.559
Some people are born fearful and inclined
to join a herd — and some are born fearless

00:01:03.559 --> 00:01:06.580
and inclined to seek lonely heights.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.860
Some of us are born sedentary and sluggish
— and some of us are born crackling with

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.520
purpose and craving adventure.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:23.780
Some, to use Nietzsche’s language, are born
to be masters, and some are born slaves.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:30.700
There is a brute biological fact here: Our
traits are evolutionarily bred into us.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:36.420
Just as a sheep cannot help but be sheepish
and a hawk cannot help but be hawkish, each

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:43.690
of us inherits from our parents a long line
of inbuilt traits.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:48.920
The master types live by strength, creativity
and independence.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:54.760
They respect power, courage,, risk-taking,
even recklessness.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:02:00.580
It is natural for them to follow their own
path no matter what, to rebel against social

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:04.920
pressure and conformity.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:09.220
And by contrast, the slave types live in conformity.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:13.409
They tend to passivity, dependence, meekness.

00:02:13.409 --> 00:02:21.430
It is natural for them to stick together for
a sense of security, as herd animals do.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:26.879
Nietzsche then turns to morality—good and
bad, right and wrong.

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:33.180
For a long time we have been taught that morality
is a matter of commandments set in stone thousands

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.849
of years ago.

00:02:34.849 --> 00:02:40.879
Not so, says Nietzsche: what we take to be
moral depends on our biological nature —and

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:47.190
different biological natures dictate different
moral codes.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:53.219
Think of it this way: If you are a sheep,
then what will seem good to you as a sheep?

00:02:53.219 --> 00:02:58.681
Being able to graze peacefully, sticking close
together with others just like you, being

00:02:58.681 --> 00:03:02.090
part of the herd, and not straying off.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:04.730
What will seem bad to you?

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:12.010
Wolves will seem bad, and anything wolf-like,
predatory, or aggressive.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.049
But what if you are a wolf?

00:03:14.049 --> 00:03:19.930
Then strength, viciousness, and contempt for
the sheep will come naturally to you and seem

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:21.299
good.

00:03:21.299 --> 00:03:26.999
There is nothing the wolves and the sheep
can agree on morally—their natures are different,

00:03:26.999 --> 00:03:32.170
as are their needs and goals, as is what feels
good to them.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:36.330
Of course, it would be good for the sheep
if they could convince the wolves to be more

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:41.819
sheep-like, but no self-respecting wolf will
fall for that.

00:03:41.819 --> 00:03:50.070
So: one’s moral code is a function of one’s
psychological makeup, and one’s psychological

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:54.599
make-up is a function of one’s biological
make-up.

00:03:54.599 --> 00:04:00.980
Nietzsche is among the first to apply evolutionary
concepts to morality: Moral codes are part

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:06.650
of a biological type’s life strategy of
survival, and the more one looks at the history

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:13.030
of morality evolutionarily and biologically,
the more one is struck by dramatic changes

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:15.409
in moral codes across time.

00:04:15.409 --> 00:04:23.620
And this is the key problem, Nietzsche argues,
for the historical record shows a disturbing

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:24.680
inversion.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:30.530
Formerly, we prized above all excellence and
power, and we looked down upon the humble

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.090
and the lowly.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:38.200
Yet now the meek, the humble, and the common
man are the “good,” while the aggressive,

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:43.020
the powerful, the strong, the proud are “evil”.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:48.390
Somehow the morality of the weak has become
dominant, and the morality of the strong has

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.950
declined.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:58.030
This moral inversion is dangerous: the traits
of strength and power, those of that ennoble

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:04.120
man, are now condemned; and the traits of
ordinariness and modesty, those of that weaken

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.930
man, are praised.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:13.380
Morality, accordingly, has become a bad thing;
or, more paradoxically, morality has become

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.780
immoral.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:20.090
The morality of the weak has somehow become
dominant, and the morality of the strong has

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.340
declined.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:28.010
How is this rather paradoxical state of affairs
to be explained?

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.930
TO BE CONTINUED

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:36.720
What are your thoughts on Nietzsche’s view
of man being born along the spectrum of sheep

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:37.840
and wolves?

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:42.240
And do you share his concern about an inversion
of moral values?

